1
00:00:37,759 --> 00:00:38,280
Oh, man!

2
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:39,320
Star reporter Shen!

3
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:40,560
Hello, hello, hello!

4
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:42,640
I'm Factory Director Ma Guowen.

5
00:00:43,119 --> 00:00:43,719
Hello, Director Ma.

6
00:00:44,439 --> 00:00:44,880
Sorry to keep you waiting.

7
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:45,840
I'll show you around first,

8
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:46,679
then you can interview me.

9
00:00:46,799 --> 00:00:47,200
Let's go, let's go.

10
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:47,560
Come on.

11
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:51,840
That's the workshop over there,

12
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:53,280
and that's my office.

13
00:00:53,359 --> 00:00:54,119
After that, you can interview me.

14
00:00:54,320 --> 00:00:55,280
Zhao Haipeng!

15
00:00:55,719 --> 00:00:57,320
It's Zhao Haipeng from Publicity.

16
00:00:57,920 --> 00:00:59,520
Come to the Area One workshop.

17
00:00:59,560 --> 00:01:00,520
Hurry up!

18
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:02,399
Zhao Haipeng!

19
00:01:02,399 --> 00:01:03,439
Rushing me like crazy... Publicity...

20
00:01:03,439 --> 00:01:04,159
Seriously... Zhao Haipeng!

21
00:01:04,359 --> 00:01:06,400
Come to the Bottling Workshop in Area One.

22
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:07,400
Hurry up!

23
00:01:11,719 --> 00:01:12,319
Comrade Reporter!

24
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:13,079
Hello!

25
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:14,760
I'm Zhao Haipeng from Publicity.

26
00:01:16,280 --> 00:01:16,840
Hello.

27
00:01:16,959 --> 00:01:18,200
Shen Leshui from Lacheng TV.

28
00:01:19,239 --> 00:01:20,239
My chain slipped off earlier.

29
00:01:22,439 --> 00:01:23,159
I mean...

30
00:01:23,239 --> 00:01:23,719
you know...

31
00:01:23,879 --> 00:01:25,159
My bike... bike chain slipped off.

32
00:01:26,519 --> 00:01:27,159
What was your name again?

33
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:28,640
Shen Leshui.

34
00:01:29,439 --> 00:01:30,519
Our Lapi Brewery,

35
00:01:30,599 --> 00:01:32,319
riding the wave of reform,

36
00:01:32,519 --> 00:01:34,200
is full of drive right now!

37
00:01:34,239 --> 00:01:35,680
Production has really ramped up.

38
00:01:36,359 --> 00:01:36,920
In a little while,

39
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:38,480
we'll all gather by the entrance,

40
00:01:38,519 --> 00:01:40,120
and take a lively group photo.

41
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:40,959
A big group photo!

42
00:01:41,159 --> 00:01:42,640
Show off our brand-new look!

43
00:01:43,159 --> 00:01:45,719
This is Cheng Youtian from Bottling.

44
00:01:46,280 --> 00:01:47,319
He does great work! "I love Lapi!"

45
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:48,799
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

46
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:49,959
Group photo, group photo!

47
00:01:50,799 --> 00:01:51,159
Quick, quick, quick!

48
00:01:51,159 --> 00:01:51,560
Well...

49
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,680
Right, our second-in-command is right!

50
00:01:54,359 --> 00:01:56,400
Let's all take a big group photo!

51
00:01:57,239 --> 00:01:58,959
Today we take the 20th century's...

52
00:01:59,079 --> 00:02:01,640
most important group photo for Lapi Brewery!

53
00:02:01,719 --> 00:02:03,079
Everyone, look happy!

54
00:02:03,079 --> 00:02:03,959
Great!

55
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:06,400
Hey, Reporter...

56
00:02:06,799 --> 00:02:07,239
Right, right.

57
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:07,959
Reporter!

58
00:02:08,039 --> 00:02:09,280
Get in the photo with us!

59
00:02:09,479 --> 00:02:10,120
We can't do it without you!

60
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:10,639
Come on, come on.

61
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:12,120
Come over here.

62
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:12,840
Join in, join in!

63
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:13,800
Stand in the middle.

64
00:02:14,439 --> 00:02:15,639
All right, follow my lead!

65
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:17,159
"Lapi is my home!"

66
00:02:17,479 --> 00:02:18,960
Ready, go!

67
00:02:19,159 --> 00:02:21,439
Lapi is my home,

68
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:24,400
and we all love it!

69
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:26,159
Yeah!

70
00:04:03,039 --> 00:04:03,639
How much do you weigh?

71
00:04:03,639 --> 00:04:04,719
About 120 to 130 jin.

72
00:04:05,319 --> 00:04:06,400
How much did Ma Guowen weigh?

73
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:07,960
About the same as me.

74
00:04:08,639 --> 00:04:10,240
Dead weight is heavier than living weight.

75
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:11,919
Don't walk.

76
00:04:12,199 --> 00:04:12,719
I won't.

77
00:04:12,719 --> 00:04:13,680
Walking ruins the reenactment.

78
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:14,800
Do you have any strength left?

79
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:15,120
Yeah.

80
00:04:15,719 --> 00:04:17,759
From the factory office to here,

81
00:04:18,319 --> 00:04:19,199
how long did it take?

82
00:04:19,399 --> 00:04:20,360
Less than 20 minutes.

83
00:04:20,759 --> 00:04:21,600
Let's stop here for now, bro.

84
00:04:25,199 --> 00:04:26,040
I can't carry you anymore.

85
00:04:26,839 --> 00:04:28,000
This guy's got incredible stamina.

86
00:04:28,759 --> 00:04:29,759
Then why did he

87
00:04:30,439 --> 00:04:31,399
spend all that time

88
00:04:31,399 --> 00:04:33,120
dragging him from the office to the tracks,

89
00:04:33,279 --> 00:04:34,959
and even posing him on his knees?

90
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:36,279
What was he after?

91
00:04:36,839 --> 00:04:38,959
Just so the train would smash him to pieces?

92
00:04:38,959 --> 00:04:39,480
Or...

93
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:41,639
did he have another motive?

94
00:04:42,560 --> 00:04:43,519
To confuse the investigation.

95
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:48,680
It snowed so heavily last night,

96
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:50,480
and the wind was blowing hard.

97
00:04:52,160 --> 00:04:53,439
Nobody comes out here.

98
00:04:54,519 --> 00:04:55,560
No eyewitnesses,

99
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:57,560
no surveillance cameras,

100
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:02,360
and the snow covered all the footprints.

101
00:05:02,959 --> 00:05:03,639
No cameras,

102
00:05:03,639 --> 00:05:04,800
no witnesses,

103
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:06,920
not even any footprints.

104
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:08,560
So we basically have no clues at all.

105
00:05:15,279 --> 00:05:16,600
The victim, Ma Guowen,

106
00:05:16,879 --> 00:05:18,240
was 58 years old,

107
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:19,759
174 centimeters tall,

108
00:05:20,199 --> 00:05:21,560
and weighed 62 kilograms.

109
00:05:22,199 --> 00:05:24,360
Comminuted fracture on the left skull.

110
00:05:24,439 --> 00:05:26,439
Congestion in both eyelids and conjunctiva.

111
00:05:26,959 --> 00:05:28,319
Edema at the margins of the conjunctiva.

112
00:05:28,959 --> 00:05:30,160
The cause of death was determined

113
00:05:30,399 --> 00:05:32,079
to be craniocerebral injury.

114
00:05:33,319 --> 00:05:34,800
The plastic bag over the victim's head

115
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:36,639
shows no signs of stretching or deformation.

116
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:38,120
Only biological traces

117
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:39,439
belonging to Ma Guowen were found on it.

118
00:05:40,199 --> 00:05:41,160
None from anyone else.

119
00:05:42,240 --> 00:05:43,560
The crime scene was also cleaned up.

120
00:05:44,519 --> 00:05:45,079
Furthermore,

121
00:05:45,079 --> 00:05:46,680
the killer was swift,

122
00:05:46,959 --> 00:05:47,600
very strong,

123
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:50,399
and had counter-investigation skills.

124
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:53,120
Given what we know about the factory,

125
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:55,639
the killer had plenty of time to strike.

126
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:58,800
According to the autopsy report,

127
00:05:58,959 --> 00:05:59,920
the victim had likely eaten

128
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:01,839
a heavy dinner shortly before he died.

129
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:04,680
Plus, there were no signs of a struggle.

130
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:06,959
That indicates

131
00:06:07,079 --> 00:06:08,319
it was someone he knew.

132
00:06:10,199 --> 00:06:12,399
Tell us about Ma Guowen's social connections.

133
00:06:13,399 --> 00:06:13,839
Right.

134
00:06:15,319 --> 00:06:15,959
Well,

135
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:17,160
Lapi Brewery

136
00:06:17,439 --> 00:06:19,199
used to be the local economic pillar.

137
00:06:19,439 --> 00:06:20,680
Back when I was in school,

138
00:06:20,839 --> 00:06:22,120
anyone working there

139
00:06:22,360 --> 00:06:23,519
was a big deal.

140
00:06:23,879 --> 00:06:25,959
So Director Ma's connections

141
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:27,480
must be quite extensive.

142
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:30,560
Based on what you just said,

143
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:33,600
and what came out

144
00:06:34,439 --> 00:06:35,360
in Ma Guowen's autopsy report,

145
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:36,879
I've summed up a few key points.

146
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:38,040
One:

147
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:40,040
it's someone he knew.

148
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:42,560
Two:

149
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:43,519
they must be physically strong.

150
00:06:44,199 --> 00:06:45,560
Three: they have a grudge.

151
00:06:45,839 --> 00:06:48,240
Four: they have counter-investigation skills.

152
00:06:48,480 --> 00:06:49,240
Someone he knew...

153
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:50,439
Who could that be?

154
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:53,240
Factory veterans?

155
00:06:53,639 --> 00:06:55,759
But there's one problem with old-timers:

156
00:06:55,959 --> 00:06:57,360
would they have the strength

157
00:06:57,759 --> 00:06:59,079
to haul Ma Guowen around?

158
00:06:59,360 --> 00:07:00,959
If they're in good shape,

159
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:02,560
they could be street thugs.

160
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:04,959
Is that a possibility?

161
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:07,120
Street thugs

162
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:08,920
holding a grudge against Ma Guowen.

163
00:07:09,399 --> 00:07:10,959
Since Ma Guowen was selling the factory,

164
00:07:11,439 --> 00:07:13,680
disputes could have flared up.

165
00:07:14,399 --> 00:07:15,279
Then again, there's another issue.

166
00:07:15,279 --> 00:07:16,199
If they're street thugs,

167
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:18,160
would they have counter-investigation skills?

168
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:18,720
Right.

169
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:20,399
Some street thugs are good at evading police,

170
00:07:20,519 --> 00:07:22,160
but from our investigation,

171
00:07:22,439 --> 00:07:25,839
this person knows the brewery inside out.

172
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:27,240
So would street thugs

173
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:28,839
really know the brewery that well,

174
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:30,800
and have those counter-investigation skills?

175
00:07:31,560 --> 00:07:33,040
Based on the points I just went through,

176
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:36,720
I've narrowed down the suspect profile.

177
00:07:37,240 --> 00:07:37,920
Let's

178
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,040
focus our search within this scope:

179
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:42,120
a physically strong male,

180
00:07:42,639 --> 00:07:44,959
connected to Ma Guowen or Lapi Brewery,

181
00:07:45,399 --> 00:07:46,519
holding a grudge.

182
00:07:47,079 --> 00:07:48,319
On top of that, the suspect

183
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:49,240
has to be sharp,

184
00:07:50,279 --> 00:07:51,480
and skilled in counter-investigation.

185
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:52,759
What do you think?

186
00:08:02,360 --> 00:08:03,480
Are bottle caps really that fun?

187
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:08,079
Are you even listening to me?

188
00:08:08,800 --> 00:08:09,759
I'm listening, bro.

189
00:08:10,759 --> 00:08:11,759
You got a different opinion?

190
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:13,120
No.

191
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:14,680
I think your analysis is spot on.

192
00:08:16,079 --> 00:08:18,040
Just one little question, though.

193
00:08:18,199 --> 00:08:20,920
I might've lost track earlier.

194
00:08:21,199 --> 00:08:23,720
How did we deduce that the suspect

195
00:08:23,720 --> 00:08:26,399
is likely a strong, able-bodied man

196
00:08:26,399 --> 00:08:27,279
with great stamina?

197
00:08:28,399 --> 00:08:29,680
Carrying you on my back,

198
00:08:30,079 --> 00:08:32,039
I hadn't even reached the tracks from the office,

199
00:08:32,039 --> 00:08:32,960
just reaching the old smokestack,

200
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:33,679
I was already completely exhausted.

201
00:08:33,679 --> 00:08:34,519
It took 20 minutes.

202
00:08:34,639 --> 00:08:36,200
How could this person not have crazy stamina?

203
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:38,120
Didn't we also mention back then

204
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:40,200
that they might've used tools?

205
00:08:40,480 --> 00:08:41,720
A handcart, a flatbed cart,

206
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:43,200
or even a car are all possible.

207
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:45,000
The snow covered everything anyway,

208
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:46,320
so we couldn't see tire tracks anyway.

209
00:08:48,480 --> 00:08:49,200
Fine, sure.

210
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:51,000
Then you go find that handcart,

211
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:52,320
flatbed cart, or car.

212
00:08:52,879 --> 00:08:53,600
Track it down.

213
00:08:54,039 --> 00:08:54,759
Anything's possible,

214
00:08:54,799 --> 00:08:55,320
right?

215
00:08:57,200 --> 00:08:57,679
Right.

216
00:08:57,919 --> 00:09:00,399
Well, the new info I have is...

217
00:09:00,399 --> 00:09:01,759
I think his MO

218
00:09:01,799 --> 00:09:02,679
is really quite unique.

219
00:09:02,759 --> 00:09:04,120
First of all, we all know

220
00:09:04,159 --> 00:09:06,399
his MO is very ritualistic.

221
00:09:06,679 --> 00:09:08,039
A bottle cap was embedded in the head.

222
00:09:08,759 --> 00:09:09,600
This bottle cap...

223
00:09:09,600 --> 00:09:10,879
Wait, aren't we discussing

224
00:09:10,960 --> 00:09:12,240
the murder weapons?

225
00:09:13,279 --> 00:09:14,519
Why are we talking about the bottle cap again?

226
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:17,159
And I already had Wenxiu look into the bottle cap.

227
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:18,960
Right.

228
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:20,679
She turned up some info.

229
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:22,840
Back in 1999,

230
00:09:23,159 --> 00:09:24,320
the brewery...

231
00:09:24,399 --> 00:09:27,039
to celebrate the millennium,

232
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:28,799
made this.

233
00:09:28,799 --> 00:09:30,320
To celebrate the coming of the new millennium,

234
00:09:30,360 --> 00:09:32,039
they put out a special commemorative edition.

235
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:34,279
And back then, they solicited

236
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:36,559
public design submissions.

237
00:09:36,679 --> 00:09:38,159
This design was chosen in the end.

238
00:09:38,399 --> 00:09:39,399
This design

239
00:09:40,039 --> 00:09:41,480
was only in circulation for one year.

240
00:09:41,480 --> 00:09:43,279
Meaning the cap on the victim's head

241
00:09:43,279 --> 00:09:44,720
has long been out of production.

242
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:46,240
They don't exist anymore.

243
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:48,440
Back in 1999,

244
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:50,000
wasn't there someone named Liu Xuemei,

245
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:50,799
a female beer taster,

246
00:09:50,879 --> 00:09:52,039
who accidentally froze to death?

247
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:53,519
Froze to death accidentally after drinking?

248
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:55,440
That was so many years ago.

249
00:09:55,679 --> 00:09:56,879
Besides, it wasn't even a case.

250
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:58,200
Because a case was never opened.

251
00:09:58,519 --> 00:09:59,519
Something from over a decade ago,

252
00:09:59,519 --> 00:10:01,600
what does it have to do with Ma Guowen's case today?

253
00:10:01,799 --> 00:10:02,600
It's connected.

254
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:03,399
Bro,

255
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:05,240
the connection between them is

256
00:10:05,559 --> 00:10:08,759
at the scene where Liu Xuemei froze to death,

257
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:11,360
there was also a bottle cap just like this.

258
00:10:11,879 --> 00:10:12,759
How do you know that?

259
00:10:12,919 --> 00:10:14,080
It was all over the news.

260
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:17,960
How old were you in '99?

261
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:20,879
Seven or eight.

262
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:23,200
A seven- or eight-year-old kid...

263
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:24,240
didn't watch cartoons,

264
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:25,480
but watched the news?

265
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:28,759
Is that what a kid that age does?

266
00:10:28,759 --> 00:10:29,080
No...

267
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:30,840
I watched cartoons back then, too.

268
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:31,200
Wait, no.

269
00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:33,399
I didn't watch that news when I was a kid.

270
00:10:33,440 --> 00:10:34,320
Then when did you watch it?

271
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:36,360
I watched it seven or eight hours ago.

272
00:10:36,519 --> 00:10:38,240
Seven or eight hours ago,

273
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:40,240
you watched news from over a decade ago?

274
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:41,639
Shen Leshui told me to watch it.

275
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:43,799
She said she represented the TV station back then

276
00:10:43,919 --> 00:10:44,679
to cover Liu Xuemei's death.

277
00:10:44,679 --> 00:10:45,639
Wait, Shen Leshui?

278
00:10:45,639 --> 00:10:47,000
When did she tell you to watch the news?

279
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:47,759
How come I didn't know?

280
00:10:48,519 --> 00:10:50,279
She told me when we questioned her that day.

281
00:10:51,159 --> 00:10:52,000
I was there when we questioned her.

282
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:52,879
I didn't hear that.

283
00:10:53,159 --> 00:10:53,840
She said it.

284
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:55,279
She didn't.

285
00:10:55,320 --> 00:10:55,960
She did.

286
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:57,279
You stepped out for a second.

287
00:10:57,440 --> 00:10:58,519
Just in that brief moment,

288
00:10:58,679 --> 00:10:59,559
she told me.

289
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:02,799
In that split second I was out,

290
00:11:03,600 --> 00:11:04,720
you two sure talked a lot.

291
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:11,879
Shen Leshui.

292
00:11:13,919 --> 00:11:15,159
Okay, I'll head over right now.

293
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:18,879
Shen Leshui

294
00:11:19,919 --> 00:11:21,080
says she received a threatening letter.

295
00:11:35,759 --> 00:11:37,840
Lapi Brewery used to be a state-owned plant.

296
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:39,399
After it was restructured,

297
00:11:39,399 --> 00:11:41,240
Director Ma Guowen bought it at auction

298
00:11:41,679 --> 00:11:42,759
and made it his own.

299
00:11:43,080 --> 00:11:44,320
Over the years,

300
00:11:44,399 --> 00:11:45,679
many workers left,

301
00:11:45,679 --> 00:11:46,759
and it shrank in size.

302
00:11:46,799 --> 00:11:47,600
Now he wanted to flip it.

303
00:11:48,519 --> 00:11:49,480
Did the killer murder him

304
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:50,559
to stop him from selling the plant?

305
00:11:53,279 --> 00:11:54,279
Stop him from selling?

306
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:56,639
Then why go through the trouble

307
00:11:56,679 --> 00:11:58,960
of moving the body to the old tracks?

308
00:12:00,879 --> 00:12:01,840
To make a scene, of course.

309
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:04,440
The bigger the fuss, the better.

310
00:12:04,639 --> 00:12:05,559
So no one would buy it.

311
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:07,200
Does that make sense?

312
00:12:08,519 --> 00:12:09,919
Hardly anyone visits the old plant.

313
00:12:10,759 --> 00:12:11,679
Leaving it at the new plant

314
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:12,440
would cause a bigger stir.

315
00:12:16,879 --> 00:12:18,039
Then that means he

316
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:20,960
knew someone would be filming that day,

317
00:12:21,559 --> 00:12:22,879
and deliberately put the body there.

318
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:25,759
So does this killer

319
00:12:25,919 --> 00:12:27,000
have any connection

320
00:12:27,879 --> 00:12:29,320
to the person filming?

321
00:12:30,080 --> 00:12:31,080
Wasn't the person filming...

322
00:12:32,039 --> 00:12:33,039
Shen Leshui?

323
00:12:34,039 --> 00:12:35,720
He wanted Shen Leshui

324
00:12:35,759 --> 00:12:37,039
to film Ma Guowen's dead body.

325
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:39,120
Bro, if you put it that way,

326
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:40,080
that's terrifying.

327
00:12:41,279 --> 00:12:42,679
Shen Leshui has been away for how many years?

328
00:12:43,080 --> 00:12:43,919
Over a decade.

329
00:12:44,080 --> 00:12:44,720
And right as she returns,

330
00:12:44,720 --> 00:12:45,480
Ma Guowen ends up dead.

331
00:12:50,519 --> 00:12:52,600
Besides, Ma Guowen asked her to film, right?

332
00:12:55,320 --> 00:12:56,639
Now she's received a threat letter.

333
00:12:58,159 --> 00:12:59,039
Let's go ask her.

334
00:13:18,279 --> 00:13:19,039
Who is it?

335
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:31,200
Leshui.

336
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:32,960
Are you all right?

337
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:35,120
Just shaken up.

338
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:38,000
Is anything missing from your home?

339
00:13:38,159 --> 00:13:39,039
No, nothing like that.

340
00:13:39,279 --> 00:13:40,240
Where's the threatening letter?

341
00:13:47,519 --> 00:13:49,279
"Don't come looking to die here.

342
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:50,960
Get lost."

343
00:13:54,919 --> 00:13:55,559
Don't be scared.

344
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:56,919
By the way...

345
00:13:56,960 --> 00:13:58,440
Who lives across the hall?

346
00:13:59,159 --> 00:13:59,720
Tu Chunyan.

347
00:14:00,159 --> 00:14:01,519
A laid-off worker from Lapi Brewery.

348
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:02,679
Last night,

349
00:14:02,679 --> 00:14:04,080
a man named Qian Yichuan came to see her.

350
00:14:04,200 --> 00:14:05,000
Qian Yichuan?

351
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:06,840
The guard from Lapi Brewery?

352
00:14:07,039 --> 00:14:08,159
The one who walks with a limp?

353
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:09,720
I don't know what he does,

354
00:14:09,720 --> 00:14:10,840
but he was here last night.

355
00:14:12,639 --> 00:14:14,080
Tu Chunyan kept dumping trash outside,

356
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:15,159
so I reported her to property management.

357
00:14:15,159 --> 00:14:15,799
She was furious,

358
00:14:16,519 --> 00:14:17,720
but she wouldn't do something like this.

359
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:19,320
Living this close would make it too obvious.

360
00:14:19,679 --> 00:14:20,960
Let me ask you something.

361
00:14:21,639 --> 00:14:23,519
Why did Ma Guowen always hire you to film?

362
00:14:24,279 --> 00:14:25,600
Back in 2000, it was you.

363
00:14:25,919 --> 00:14:27,080
Then over ten years passed,

364
00:14:27,080 --> 00:14:28,200
and the moment you returned, he hired you again.

365
00:14:28,600 --> 00:14:30,440
Do you two have some special connection?

366
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:33,000
Also, he gave you 30,000 yuan.

367
00:14:33,279 --> 00:14:35,360
Did you write an IOU or sign a receipt?

368
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:36,519
You shouldn't be asking me that.

369
00:14:36,519 --> 00:14:37,440
You should ask him.

370
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:38,840
Isn't he dead?

371
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:41,080
Only you know why he kept reaching out to you.

372
00:14:41,799 --> 00:14:43,559
First of all, he didn't keep reaching out to me.

373
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:44,759
Over ten years ago,

374
00:14:44,759 --> 00:14:46,279
it was an assignment from Lacheng TV.

375
00:14:46,279 --> 00:14:47,399
I barely knew him.

376
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:49,360
This time, we bumped into each other on the street.

377
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:52,759
Bumped into each other?

378
00:14:54,039 --> 00:14:54,840
What a coincidence.

379
00:15:01,039 --> 00:15:01,519
Leshui.

380
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:04,720
Did Ma Guowen ever mention

381
00:15:04,720 --> 00:15:06,120
wanting aerial shots,

382
00:15:06,200 --> 00:15:08,440
or filming the railroad tracks?

383
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:10,320
He never mentioned the tracks.

384
00:15:11,120 --> 00:15:12,600
Aerial shots made him really excited, though.

385
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,039
He insisted on getting aerial footage.

386
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:15,759
And then you happened to capture it.

387
00:15:15,799 --> 00:15:16,519
Officer Han,

388
00:15:16,840 --> 00:15:18,480
do you also think Ma Guowen's death

389
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:19,399
has something to do with me?

390
00:15:19,639 --> 00:15:21,440
Or that I shouldn't be seeking protection,

391
00:15:21,519 --> 00:15:22,559
but should be suspected instead?

392
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:23,639
No.

393
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:24,480
Never suspected you.

394
00:15:24,639 --> 00:15:26,200
Your ex-husband Zhao Haipeng,

395
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:27,519
the gatekeeper Qian Yichuan,

396
00:15:27,519 --> 00:15:29,440
and the forklift driver Cao Jun—

397
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:31,279
after the factory was restructured,

398
00:15:31,320 --> 00:15:32,320
they all stepped down as old workers.

399
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:34,120
They probably didn't get along with Ma Guowen.

400
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,559
Haven't you caught up with them since you returned?

401
00:15:37,519 --> 00:15:40,320
You know these old Lapi Brewery workers quite well.

402
00:15:40,679 --> 00:15:41,639
Do you have relatives here?

403
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:46,919
Just doing my job.

404
00:15:51,279 --> 00:15:52,120
Look at this.

405
00:15:52,440 --> 00:15:53,799
"Get out of Lapi Brewery Compound."

406
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:56,120
Who do you think wants you to leave?

407
00:15:57,039 --> 00:15:57,559
Could it be that back then,

408
00:15:57,559 --> 00:15:59,240
you offended someone while shooting the documentary?

409
00:15:59,440 --> 00:16:00,519
How would I know?

410
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:01,799
By the way,

411
00:16:02,279 --> 00:16:04,279
in the footage I shot,

412
00:16:04,279 --> 00:16:05,600
did you find any clues?

413
00:16:05,879 --> 00:16:07,360
Did the suspect leave any traces?

414
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:08,919
I can't disclose that right now.

415
00:16:11,799 --> 00:16:13,240
I just want to know a bit more

416
00:16:13,240 --> 00:16:15,039
about the progress of Ma Guowen's case,

417
00:16:15,039 --> 00:16:16,879
out of concern for my own safety.

418
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:17,399
Understood.

419
00:16:17,399 --> 00:16:17,879
After all...

420
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:24,240
These are my personal belongings.

421
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:26,759
Sorry about that.

422
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:29,240
Lately, whenever I see black trash bags,

423
00:16:29,240 --> 00:16:30,120
I get a bit on edge.

424
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:31,360
What's in here?

425
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:32,159
Can I take a look?

426
00:16:33,279 --> 00:16:33,919
Raw footage tapes.

427
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:36,080
May I take a look?

428
00:16:43,879 --> 00:16:45,159
Such precious raw footage,

429
00:16:45,159 --> 00:16:46,320
and you usually keep it in

430
00:16:46,320 --> 00:16:47,240
a black garbage bag like this?

431
00:16:47,480 --> 00:16:48,120
Yeah, I do.

432
00:16:48,320 --> 00:16:49,279
I've always kept it in here.

433
00:16:51,519 --> 00:16:52,360
Real classy.

434
00:16:55,120 --> 00:16:56,960
Unused footage from "Malt Kingdom"...

435
00:16:58,480 --> 00:16:59,440
All of these?

436
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:01,759
Then there must be plenty of footage of Ma Guowen

437
00:17:01,759 --> 00:17:03,840
and the others in here.

438
00:17:04,319 --> 00:17:05,599
And around Millennium Eve,

439
00:17:05,599 --> 00:17:06,759
you went to shoot footage too, right?

440
00:17:07,440 --> 00:17:09,000
Does this have anything to do with me being threatened?

441
00:17:09,519 --> 00:17:10,559
Of course it does.

442
00:17:11,240 --> 00:17:12,640
Look, both times you filmed,

443
00:17:13,079 --> 00:17:15,839
it was right when the factory was being sold,

444
00:17:16,559 --> 00:17:17,680
and people ended up dead both times.

445
00:17:18,359 --> 00:17:19,279
Quite a coincidence.

446
00:17:20,039 --> 00:17:20,519
Tell you what,

447
00:17:20,839 --> 00:17:21,720
this stuff...

448
00:17:22,119 --> 00:17:23,359
We'll take it back to examine first,

449
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:24,880
to see if there are any leads.

450
00:17:25,680 --> 00:17:26,319
No way.

451
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:28,640
The tape is damaged.

452
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:29,759
It won't play.

453
00:17:30,880 --> 00:17:31,359
We can...

454
00:17:31,359 --> 00:17:33,240
get a professional technician to fix it for you.

455
00:17:33,759 --> 00:17:35,119
If it's ruined, you can't afford to pay me back.

456
00:17:35,160 --> 00:17:36,880
If it gets ruined, how much should we pay you?

457
00:17:36,920 --> 00:17:37,720
It's priceless.

458
00:17:45,079 --> 00:17:45,799
Xiao Gao,

459
00:17:48,319 --> 00:17:49,119
did you bring evidence bags?

460
00:17:52,960 --> 00:17:54,039
Take all those threatening letters.

461
00:17:55,160 --> 00:17:56,160
Just the threatening letters?

462
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:57,880
Nothing else?

463
00:17:58,519 --> 00:17:59,400
How about I take you in too?

464
00:18:05,599 --> 00:18:06,359
Well...

465
00:18:07,799 --> 00:18:09,960
He just wants to understand the situation better.

466
00:18:11,279 --> 00:18:11,680
You know,

467
00:18:11,680 --> 00:18:12,519
asking in detail

468
00:18:12,559 --> 00:18:13,519
helps solve the case.

469
00:18:15,279 --> 00:18:15,759
Listen,

470
00:18:15,799 --> 00:18:17,160
keep your door locked at home,

471
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:19,079
keep your phone charged,

472
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:20,160
and if anything happens,

473
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:21,720
just call me like you did today.

474
00:18:25,640 --> 00:18:26,480
Thanks for your cooperation.

475
00:18:30,319 --> 00:18:30,880
We're heading out.

476
00:18:41,599 --> 00:18:42,160
Xiao Gao,

477
00:18:43,960 --> 00:18:46,200
when you worked cases with Qiang in Qingzhou,

478
00:18:46,200 --> 00:18:47,079
were you like this too?

479
00:18:48,039 --> 00:18:49,160
Running your mouth non-stop?

480
00:18:49,720 --> 00:18:50,799
Before the boss could even finish,

481
00:18:50,960 --> 00:18:52,279
you jumped in and said it all.

482
00:18:54,440 --> 00:18:56,119
I didn't use to talk so much.

483
00:18:56,480 --> 00:18:57,480
Brother Qiang insisted I speak up.

484
00:18:57,480 --> 00:18:58,839
If... If I didn't, he'd kick me.

485
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:00,000
He even kicked you?

486
00:19:00,920 --> 00:19:02,039
Wasn't that for my own good?

487
00:19:02,119 --> 00:19:03,599
Now I'm all trained up.

488
00:19:04,519 --> 00:19:05,720
Mind your approach a bit.

489
00:19:06,599 --> 00:19:07,440
She's a victim.

490
00:19:08,119 --> 00:19:09,920
You can't turn her place into an interrogation room.

491
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:13,599
The questions I asked

492
00:19:13,640 --> 00:19:15,359
were all related to her case.

493
00:19:16,119 --> 00:19:17,480
Who sent the threatening letters,

494
00:19:17,720 --> 00:19:19,039
why they wanted her to leave here,

495
00:19:19,519 --> 00:19:20,960
and earlier downstairs,

496
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:22,440
when we analyzed why Ma Guowen

497
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:24,000
always picked her to film.

498
00:19:24,039 --> 00:19:25,240
She didn't give clear answers to any of it.

499
00:19:26,119 --> 00:19:27,240
And that raw footage tape.

500
00:19:27,920 --> 00:19:29,279
Did you see that earlier, bro?

501
00:19:29,440 --> 00:19:30,799
The second I touched it, she snatched it back.

502
00:19:31,119 --> 00:19:32,240
There's definitely information on it.

503
00:19:32,599 --> 00:19:33,839
Why was she afraid to let us see it?

504
00:19:34,519 --> 00:19:36,039
Still, you can't just snatch it from her.

505
00:19:39,319 --> 00:19:40,240
Either way, I'm sure

506
00:19:40,559 --> 00:19:41,720
there are clues we need in there.

507
00:19:42,359 --> 00:19:43,240
Next chance I get,

508
00:19:43,240 --> 00:19:44,079
I'm asking her for it again.

509
00:19:45,839 --> 00:19:47,519
Did you notice anything else?

510
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:50,599
Your shoe covers.

511
00:19:52,160 --> 00:19:52,920
It's snowing.

512
00:19:53,079 --> 00:19:54,160
Watch out, it's slippery.

513
00:19:59,960 --> 00:20:01,000
Didn't you lock the car?

514
00:20:02,559 --> 00:20:03,960
It acts up in this cold.

515
00:20:34,200 --> 00:20:36,759
Did he mention anything about aerial shots,

516
00:20:36,839 --> 00:20:38,759
or filming the railroad tracks?

517
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:40,920
He didn't mention the tracks.

518
00:20:41,759 --> 00:20:43,279
Aerial shots really got him excited, though.

519
00:20:43,279 --> 00:20:44,240
He insisted on getting aerial shots.

520
00:20:44,599 --> 00:20:46,160
And then you captured it.

521
00:20:46,480 --> 00:20:47,119
Officer Han,

522
00:20:47,640 --> 00:20:49,400
do you think Ma Guowen's death

523
00:20:49,400 --> 00:20:50,319
has something to do with me?

524
00:20:50,319 --> 00:20:51,960
Or that I shouldn't be seeking protection,

525
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:53,039
but should be suspected instead?

526
00:20:53,599 --> 00:20:54,119
No.

527
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:55,000
We don't suspect you.

528
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:55,680
We're just...

529
00:21:19,680 --> 00:21:20,880
You're in the news business.

530
00:21:21,039 --> 00:21:21,599
Investigating someone...

531
00:21:21,599 --> 00:21:22,880
why are you asking me for help?

532
00:21:23,279 --> 00:21:24,359
I don't have those skills.

533
00:21:24,559 --> 00:21:25,759
How about I introduce you to someone?

534
00:21:29,400 --> 00:21:30,319
Is he reliable?

535
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:36,759
Chen, long time no see.

536
00:21:37,960 --> 00:21:38,880
Long time no see.

537
00:21:39,799 --> 00:21:41,119
Why are you back so early today?

538
00:21:41,359 --> 00:21:43,200
Didn't you say the station had an event tonight?

539
00:21:43,960 --> 00:21:45,480
I came back early to see Xiaohu.

540
00:21:46,160 --> 00:21:46,880
I'll let you two talk.

541
00:21:50,279 --> 00:21:51,279
How thoughtful.

542
00:21:51,880 --> 00:21:52,960
Tonight's the station anniversary.

543
00:21:53,680 --> 00:21:55,200
Everyone from the news department will be there.

544
00:21:55,519 --> 00:21:57,160
There's a guy named Li Mingyang who's pretty reliable.

545
00:21:58,400 --> 00:21:59,000
All right.

546
00:21:59,839 --> 00:22:00,519
Let's do that, then.

547
00:22:15,759 --> 00:22:16,759
Brother Chuang, have you been waiting long?

548
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:18,599
No worries, it's fine.

549
00:22:19,160 --> 00:22:19,799
Wanna ask you something.

550
00:22:20,119 --> 00:22:20,599
Go ahead.

551
00:22:21,359 --> 00:22:22,440
Do you know Ma...

552
00:22:27,160 --> 00:22:28,559
You're no good, and neither is your car.

553
00:22:30,319 --> 00:22:30,880
Brother Chuang.

554
00:22:31,119 --> 00:22:32,720
What were... What were you saying about Ma who?

555
00:22:34,240 --> 00:22:36,160
I wanted to ask about Ma Guowen.

556
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:38,680
Do you know who he offended recently?

557
00:22:39,079 --> 00:22:39,880
Who he offended?

558
00:22:41,039 --> 00:22:41,839
No idea.

559
00:22:42,160 --> 00:22:42,599
Anyway,

560
00:22:42,920 --> 00:22:44,279
that Ma Guowen,

561
00:22:44,599 --> 00:22:46,279
don't let his smiling face fool you.

562
00:22:46,279 --> 00:22:47,400
He's actually ruthless.

563
00:22:47,880 --> 00:22:50,000
Did you forget what happened to Lao Qian's leg?

564
00:22:51,119 --> 00:22:51,519
Besides,

565
00:22:51,519 --> 00:22:52,559
he's greedy and lecherous.

566
00:22:53,559 --> 00:22:54,119
Ma Guowen...

567
00:22:55,200 --> 00:22:56,680
did he clash with anyone recently?

568
00:22:57,680 --> 00:22:58,279
Cao Jun, obviously.

569
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:04,119
The night before last at 11:00 PM,

570
00:23:04,319 --> 00:23:05,160
what were you doing?

571
00:23:06,759 --> 00:23:07,720
Nothing.

572
00:23:08,200 --> 00:23:09,920
I usually don't go out after 11:00.

573
00:23:10,359 --> 00:23:11,200
I was at home.

574
00:23:11,880 --> 00:23:12,319
Right.

575
00:23:12,440 --> 00:23:13,079
At... at home.

576
00:23:13,880 --> 00:23:15,519
Can you describe what you were doing at home?

577
00:23:22,440 --> 00:23:23,119
Eating.

578
00:23:23,880 --> 00:23:25,160
Drinking, watching TV.

579
00:23:26,440 --> 00:23:27,680
Went... went to the bathroom.

580
00:23:28,160 --> 00:23:29,079
That's... that's about it.

581
00:23:30,559 --> 00:23:31,440
Three days ago, didn't you

582
00:23:31,440 --> 00:23:32,480
get into a fight with Ma Guowen?

583
00:23:34,440 --> 00:23:35,480
Who... who said that?

584
00:23:35,599 --> 00:23:36,240
Who are you asking?

585
00:23:36,559 --> 00:23:37,440
I'm asking you.

586
00:23:37,839 --> 00:23:39,839
We know you had a clash with Ma Guowen.

587
00:23:39,839 --> 00:23:40,960
You went to see him three days ago.

588
00:23:41,440 --> 00:23:42,400
Did you two get physical?

589
00:23:42,559 --> 00:23:43,240
No, no, no.

590
00:23:43,359 --> 00:23:43,839
We didn't fight.

591
00:23:43,839 --> 00:23:45,160
We just... just argued a bit.

592
00:23:45,200 --> 00:23:46,319
No, no, no hands were thrown.

593
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:47,599
After that,

594
00:23:47,799 --> 00:23:48,680
I never saw him again.

595
00:23:49,079 --> 00:23:50,079
What did you do the night before last?

596
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:53,240
I... I don't know.

597
00:23:53,319 --> 00:23:53,920
The... the night before last...

598
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:55,160
Weren't you watching TV at home?

599
00:23:55,319 --> 00:23:56,519
Eating, using the bathroom?

600
00:23:56,759 --> 00:23:57,279
That was...

601
00:23:57,359 --> 00:23:58,440
That was three... three nights ago.

602
00:23:58,640 --> 00:24:00,400
Didn't you go find Ma Guowen three nights ago?

603
00:24:03,839 --> 00:24:04,359
I...

604
00:24:04,720 --> 00:24:05,440
I... I... I...

605
00:24:05,920 --> 00:24:07,799
I... I can't really remember.

606
00:24:09,880 --> 00:24:10,279
Cao Jun.

607
00:24:10,279 --> 00:24:11,720
Playing dumb with me, are you?

608
00:24:12,200 --> 00:24:12,799
Let me tell you,

609
00:24:13,400 --> 00:24:14,839
we have all the time in the world to help you remember.

610
00:24:15,119 --> 00:24:15,960
Just sit there and think real hard.

611
00:24:43,559 --> 00:24:44,839
When did you start hauling cargo?

612
00:24:46,519 --> 00:24:47,200
Me?

613
00:24:47,599 --> 00:24:49,160
Started right after I left the factory.

614
00:24:49,599 --> 00:24:50,519
Kept at it ever since.

615
00:24:50,880 --> 00:24:52,000
We looked into it.

616
00:24:53,039 --> 00:24:54,880
Ever since Ma Guowen bought the factory,

617
00:24:55,119 --> 00:24:56,039
you've held a grudge against him.

618
00:24:56,759 --> 00:24:58,119
You went to help him move things,

619
00:24:58,720 --> 00:24:59,720
and smashed them up.

620
00:24:59,960 --> 00:25:00,359
Right?

621
00:25:00,720 --> 00:25:01,680
Ma Guowen chewed you out.

622
00:25:02,160 --> 00:25:02,920
Did that happen or not?

623
00:25:04,079 --> 00:25:05,680
I didn't break that stuff!

624
00:25:05,680 --> 00:25:06,240
Th-That...

625
00:25:06,519 --> 00:25:08,079
Ma Guowen framed me, he did!

626
00:25:08,240 --> 00:25:09,799
I don't care if he framed you

627
00:25:10,240 --> 00:25:11,359
or if you smashed it.

628
00:25:11,559 --> 00:25:12,319
It happened, didn't it?

629
00:25:13,839 --> 00:25:14,640
Cao Jun.

630
00:25:14,960 --> 00:25:16,400
I've jogged your memory enough.

631
00:25:16,519 --> 00:25:17,599
I'll ask you one more time.

632
00:25:19,720 --> 00:25:21,319
What were you doing the night before last?

633
00:25:23,880 --> 00:25:24,519
I...

634
00:25:26,480 --> 00:25:27,680
The night before last, I...

635
00:25:29,200 --> 00:25:29,680
The night before last...

636
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:30,400
Right, right.

637
00:25:30,400 --> 00:25:31,559
I wasn't at home.

638
00:25:31,599 --> 00:25:32,599
Didn't... didn't go to the restroom.

639
00:25:32,599 --> 00:25:34,079
And I didn't go see Ma Guowen either.

640
00:25:34,079 --> 00:25:34,400
I...

641
00:25:34,920 --> 00:25:35,599
I, I, I...

642
00:25:35,960 --> 00:25:36,759
I was picking up fares.

643
00:25:37,599 --> 00:25:38,640
I was picking up fares on Guangyuan Road.

644
00:25:38,640 --> 00:25:39,400
I remember now.

645
00:25:39,839 --> 00:25:41,160
Right, lots of restaurants there,

646
00:25:41,200 --> 00:25:42,200
so there were plenty of passengers.

647
00:25:42,240 --> 00:25:44,119
I converted my little tricycle into a tuk-tuk!

648
00:25:44,200 --> 00:25:45,880
I was picking up fares on Guangyuan Road that night!

649
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:46,400
Right, right, right.

650
00:25:46,400 --> 00:25:47,160
Ju-Just picking up fares.

651
00:25:47,240 --> 00:25:47,839
Are you sure?

652
00:25:47,880 --> 00:25:48,519
S-Sure! Absolutely sure.

653
00:25:48,519 --> 00:25:48,960
Picking up fares.

654
00:25:48,960 --> 00:25:49,759
Picking up fares on Guangyuan Road.

655
00:25:49,960 --> 00:25:51,240
Can anyone vouch for that?

656
00:25:59,240 --> 00:26:00,480
Look, Officer...

657
00:26:00,519 --> 00:26:02,279
You keep circling back to that night.

658
00:26:02,759 --> 00:26:03,920
Aren't you just trying to...

659
00:26:04,160 --> 00:26:04,799
You think that I...

660
00:26:04,880 --> 00:26:06,160
that I killed Ma Guowen?

661
00:26:06,240 --> 00:26:07,440
I didn't kill him!

662
00:26:07,599 --> 00:26:08,119
I wanted to, sure,

663
00:26:08,119 --> 00:26:09,880
but I didn't have the guts to kill Ma Guowen!

664
00:26:09,920 --> 00:26:11,000
Who said you killed Ma Guowen?

665
00:26:11,119 --> 00:26:11,960
Did I say that?

666
00:26:12,599 --> 00:26:13,799
You just blurted it out yourself.

667
00:26:22,680 --> 00:26:23,680
Let me ask you something.

668
00:26:24,039 --> 00:26:24,960
Do you know Shen Leshui well?

669
00:26:28,599 --> 00:26:29,839
You must be Li Mingyang.

670
00:26:30,359 --> 00:26:31,200
I'm Shen Leshui.

671
00:26:31,480 --> 00:26:31,880
Xiaoqin's friend.

672
00:26:31,880 --> 00:26:32,359
Here's some water.

673
00:26:35,000 --> 00:26:35,519
So...

674
00:26:35,799 --> 00:26:37,079
Can I sit here, Ms. Shen?

675
00:26:38,880 --> 00:26:39,240
Have a seat.

676
00:26:43,359 --> 00:26:45,200
I really didn't expect to run into you here.

677
00:26:45,799 --> 00:26:47,200
You've always been an idol of mine.

678
00:26:47,799 --> 00:26:48,680
Joining the TV station...

679
00:26:48,680 --> 00:26:49,960
I was just following in your footsteps.

680
00:26:50,400 --> 00:26:51,200
You're exaggerating.

681
00:26:51,319 --> 00:26:52,200
I'm nobody special.

682
00:26:52,440 --> 00:26:53,240
You're too modest.

683
00:26:53,759 --> 00:26:54,640
Lately,

684
00:26:54,720 --> 00:26:56,200
I've been covering social issues.

685
00:26:56,400 --> 00:26:58,359
I know you used to cover them too.

686
00:26:59,839 --> 00:27:01,680
Social issues are tough to report on.

687
00:27:02,119 --> 00:27:03,000
They really are.

688
00:27:05,359 --> 00:27:06,839
Reporting on social issues...

689
00:27:06,839 --> 00:27:07,880
You need to stick to the facts,

690
00:27:07,880 --> 00:27:09,160
be sharp and insightful,

691
00:27:09,200 --> 00:27:10,200
reveal life as it truly is,

692
00:27:10,519 --> 00:27:11,599
and have conviction,

693
00:27:11,599 --> 00:27:12,599
warmth, and passion.

694
00:27:12,799 --> 00:27:14,880
If you can't balance all three,

695
00:27:14,960 --> 00:27:16,200
it'll all crash and burn.

696
00:27:16,839 --> 00:27:17,680
"Crash and burn."

697
00:27:19,559 --> 00:27:20,960
That's quite a funny way to put it.

698
00:27:21,759 --> 00:27:23,359
I'm crashing and burning right now.

699
00:27:23,720 --> 00:27:24,559
You've got to be kidding.

700
00:27:24,599 --> 00:27:25,559
If you're going down,

701
00:27:25,559 --> 00:27:27,400
rookies like us wouldn't stand a chance.

702
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:28,799
Are you a local?

703
00:27:29,240 --> 00:27:29,799
No.

704
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:30,839
I'm from Qingzhou.

705
00:27:31,160 --> 00:27:32,119
Qingzhou, huh?

706
00:27:32,440 --> 00:27:33,359
How old are you?

707
00:27:33,480 --> 00:27:34,559
I'm 25 this year.

708
00:27:35,160 --> 00:27:35,799
What's wrong?

709
00:27:36,160 --> 00:27:37,880
I wanted to ask about someone.

710
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:38,640
Who is it?

711
00:27:42,079 --> 00:27:43,160
Actually...

712
00:27:43,759 --> 00:27:45,079
I'm looking for someone.

713
00:27:45,240 --> 00:27:46,799
Tell you what, the person you're looking for...

714
00:27:46,799 --> 00:27:48,000
Just tell me their name.

715
00:27:50,640 --> 00:27:52,039
They're at your TV station.

716
00:27:52,680 --> 00:27:53,519
In our news department?

717
00:27:57,559 --> 00:27:58,480
As for him,

718
00:27:58,720 --> 00:27:59,519
he's not a bad guy.

719
00:28:00,079 --> 00:28:01,319
I just want to know

720
00:28:02,240 --> 00:28:03,559
who his parents are

721
00:28:03,559 --> 00:28:04,240
and where his home is.

722
00:28:05,559 --> 00:28:06,440
His home? His parents?

723
00:28:06,759 --> 00:28:08,559
You're helping a kid find their parents?

724
00:28:10,599 --> 00:28:11,039
Yes.

725
00:28:11,480 --> 00:28:12,880
That's a good thing, Sister Shen!

726
00:28:13,279 --> 00:28:14,319
Then just give me the child's

727
00:28:14,519 --> 00:28:15,559
name, gender, and age.

728
00:28:15,559 --> 00:28:16,359
Just tell me all that.

729
00:28:21,240 --> 00:28:22,000
I know, Sister Shen.

730
00:28:22,960 --> 00:28:24,039
This has to stay confidential.

731
00:28:24,279 --> 00:28:25,200
That's what matters most.

732
00:28:25,480 --> 00:28:25,880
Right?

733
00:28:26,039 --> 00:28:26,640
Don't worry.

734
00:28:26,880 --> 00:28:27,880
I won't let you down.

735
00:28:29,559 --> 00:28:30,000
All right.

736
00:28:31,240 --> 00:28:31,799
Shen Leshui,

737
00:28:32,640 --> 00:28:34,119
the female reporter who filmed

738
00:28:34,119 --> 00:28:35,039
that documentary back then...

739
00:28:38,960 --> 00:28:40,359
Yeah, there was someone like that.

740
00:28:40,799 --> 00:28:41,720
She interviewed me.

741
00:28:43,799 --> 00:28:45,559
When you workers gathered together

742
00:28:45,720 --> 00:28:46,680
to discuss buying the factory,

743
00:28:47,160 --> 00:28:48,519
all the way up to the auction,

744
00:28:48,880 --> 00:28:50,799
did she record the whole process on camera?

745
00:28:52,319 --> 00:28:52,839
She did.

746
00:28:53,680 --> 00:28:54,160
Whatever we said,

747
00:28:54,160 --> 00:28:55,160
she... she recorded it all.

748
00:29:05,079 --> 00:29:06,640
I've narrowed down our suspect pool:

749
00:29:07,400 --> 00:29:08,839
an able-bodied male

750
00:29:09,400 --> 00:29:11,440
connected to Ma Guowen or Lapi Brewery.

751
00:29:11,920 --> 00:29:12,599
Someone he knew,

752
00:29:13,079 --> 00:29:13,960
with a personal grudge.

753
00:29:14,559 --> 00:29:15,480
And what's more,

754
00:29:15,599 --> 00:29:16,880
has strong counter-investigation skills.

755
00:29:47,759 --> 00:29:48,160
Old Cao.

756
00:29:48,839 --> 00:29:49,400
You're here.

757
00:29:50,720 --> 00:29:51,400
Cold out there, huh?

758
00:30:24,519 --> 00:30:25,599
I won't— I'm not drinking his stuff.

759
00:30:26,160 --> 00:30:27,079
Don't be so eccentric.

760
00:30:38,839 --> 00:30:39,759
Everyone's here.

761
00:30:40,839 --> 00:30:41,359
You're here, Haipeng.

762
00:30:41,359 --> 00:30:41,880
Sit, sit, sit.

763
00:30:44,279 --> 00:30:45,000
What's up?

764
00:30:45,799 --> 00:30:46,720
Thought you weren't showing up?

765
00:30:46,720 --> 00:30:47,400
What?

766
00:30:47,559 --> 00:30:48,000
So what if I came out?

767
00:30:48,160 --> 00:30:49,079
What?

768
00:30:49,240 --> 00:30:50,079
Come on, Old Qian.

769
00:30:50,799 --> 00:30:52,400
Drinking here at Old Cheng's,

770
00:30:52,640 --> 00:30:53,480
and you brought your own booze?

771
00:30:56,160 --> 00:30:57,319
I just like this stuff, so what?

772
00:30:58,640 --> 00:31:00,039
Fine, he's just eccentric like that.

773
00:31:00,079 --> 00:31:00,720
Why even bother talking to him?

774
00:31:01,680 --> 00:31:02,559
He's busy these days,

775
00:31:03,240 --> 00:31:04,200
guarding the factory gate.

776
00:31:05,200 --> 00:31:08,079
Only him and Tieping are still factory workers.

777
00:31:09,000 --> 00:31:09,880
Tieping's got it good.

778
00:31:10,559 --> 00:31:11,680
He has an employment contract.

779
00:31:12,720 --> 00:31:14,039
I've always been a temp.

780
00:31:16,200 --> 00:31:17,559
Back in that old factory,

781
00:31:17,599 --> 00:31:18,440
there's just a pile of scrap.

782
00:31:18,480 --> 00:31:19,480
I just sit there watching it.

783
00:31:20,799 --> 00:31:21,519
Fair enough.

784
00:31:22,039 --> 00:31:22,720
Pretty fitting.

785
00:31:23,680 --> 00:31:24,599
Junk watching junk.

786
00:31:27,720 --> 00:31:29,079
Guess what that guy...

787
00:31:29,079 --> 00:31:30,160
what Ma Guowen told me a while back?

788
00:31:31,079 --> 00:31:31,759
Ma Guowen said,

789
00:31:32,160 --> 00:31:32,799
"Old Qian,

790
00:31:33,440 --> 00:31:34,880
you guarding the gate now,

791
00:31:34,960 --> 00:31:36,559
compared to when you were an accountant,

792
00:31:37,160 --> 00:31:38,799
contributes way more to our factory."

793
00:31:39,880 --> 00:31:40,960
I was like, "How so?"

794
00:31:42,680 --> 00:31:43,359
He said,

795
00:31:44,559 --> 00:31:46,319
"'Cause you've got a disability card now."

796
00:31:50,400 --> 00:31:51,279
That Ma Guowen,

797
00:31:51,599 --> 00:31:52,559
what a piece of shit.

798
00:31:53,759 --> 00:31:55,000
Serves him right getting killed.

799
00:31:57,680 --> 00:31:58,240
Haipeng,

800
00:31:59,400 --> 00:32:00,759
your ex-wife reported the crime.

801
00:32:03,839 --> 00:32:05,240
Making big moves right after she's back.

802
00:32:07,279 --> 00:32:08,079
Didn't they even

803
00:32:08,079 --> 00:32:09,279
haul me in for questioning?

804
00:32:10,240 --> 00:32:10,759
Cao Jun.

805
00:32:11,599 --> 00:32:11,960
Here.

806
00:32:13,759 --> 00:32:14,440
Calm your nerves.

807
00:32:19,680 --> 00:32:21,640
Who killed Ma Guowen anyway?

808
00:32:25,559 --> 00:32:26,599
Do you even need to guess?

809
00:32:32,920 --> 00:32:33,720
You did, obviously.

810
00:32:49,680 --> 00:32:50,079
Come on.

811
00:32:50,119 --> 00:32:51,200
Let's toast Old Qian.

812
00:32:51,279 --> 00:32:52,079
Cheers, cheers!

813
00:32:53,680 --> 00:32:54,160
Come on, Ping.

814
00:33:00,720 --> 00:33:01,359
Don't laugh.

815
00:33:01,400 --> 00:33:02,160
What are you laughing at?

816
00:33:02,759 --> 00:33:03,039
No, really.

817
00:33:03,720 --> 00:33:04,519
Old Qian, come on, over here.

818
00:33:04,559 --> 00:33:05,119
Tell us, tell us.

819
00:33:05,920 --> 00:33:07,160
Walk us through the crime.

820
00:33:07,960 --> 00:33:08,599
How'd you kill 'em?

821
00:33:28,519 --> 00:33:29,079
Who killed him?

822
00:33:46,480 --> 00:33:48,240
I dream of being the one.

823
00:33:49,240 --> 00:33:50,559
If the case ever gets solved,

824
00:33:50,599 --> 00:33:51,440
and I catch that punk,

825
00:33:51,440 --> 00:33:52,640
I'll slap him twice first.

826
00:33:53,759 --> 00:33:55,000
He stole my gig!

827
00:33:56,720 --> 00:33:58,000
Tell me, didn't Ma Guowen have it coming?

828
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:00,880
Let's not go too far,

829
00:34:05,000 --> 00:34:05,839
look at Cao Jun.

830
00:34:07,880 --> 00:34:09,239
He won Model Worker several times, right?

831
00:34:09,320 --> 00:34:10,039
Just twice.

832
00:34:10,159 --> 00:34:11,239
Right, twice.

833
00:34:11,960 --> 00:34:12,880
I remember it clear as day.

834
00:34:13,559 --> 00:34:14,679
I handed you the bonus myself.

835
00:34:16,159 --> 00:34:17,320
Look at him now.

836
00:34:18,519 --> 00:34:19,679
If it weren't for Ma Guowen,

837
00:34:20,119 --> 00:34:20,960
and that...

838
00:34:22,039 --> 00:34:23,440
that tramp Liu Xuemei,

839
00:34:23,679 --> 00:34:24,920
would things ever come to this?

840
00:34:24,920 --> 00:34:25,559
Come on, stop.

841
00:34:25,800 --> 00:34:26,480
We were talking about Ma Guowen.

842
00:34:26,480 --> 00:34:27,480
Why drag Liu Xuemei into this?

843
00:34:27,599 --> 00:34:28,599
Why do you keep bringing her up?

844
00:34:28,639 --> 00:34:29,400
Yeah, why bring her up?

845
00:34:29,400 --> 00:34:30,039
If you want to say something,

846
00:34:30,039 --> 00:34:31,280
just say it already!

847
00:34:31,480 --> 00:34:32,000
Alright, alright.

848
00:34:32,000 --> 00:34:32,360
What?

849
00:34:32,360 --> 00:34:33,800
Driving a forklift or a tuk-tuk...

850
00:34:34,079 --> 00:34:34,880
Just drop it.

851
00:34:34,880 --> 00:34:35,559
You've had enough.

852
00:34:35,840 --> 00:34:37,280
He drinks all day long.

853
00:34:37,320 --> 00:34:38,559
Drinks liquor like water.

854
00:34:39,039 --> 00:34:39,480
Total drunkard.

855
00:34:39,480 --> 00:34:40,480
Just ignore him.

856
00:34:50,599 --> 00:34:51,360
Either way,

857
00:34:51,360 --> 00:34:52,039
let me make my stance clear.

858
00:34:52,920 --> 00:34:54,800
No matter who killed Ma Guowen,

859
00:34:57,199 --> 00:34:58,199
he's like a father to me.

860
00:35:07,639 --> 00:35:08,239
Go ahead.

861
00:35:15,199 --> 00:35:16,199
The reason I asked Cao Jun that

862
00:35:16,199 --> 00:35:16,639
was just

863
00:35:16,760 --> 00:35:18,320
to find out what happened back then.

864
00:35:23,760 --> 00:35:25,000
Right now,

865
00:35:25,280 --> 00:35:27,119
I'm really intrigued by this seven-year-old kid.

866
00:35:30,599 --> 00:35:31,519
Bro, I'm just wondering,

867
00:35:31,519 --> 00:35:32,400
does this kid

868
00:35:32,800 --> 00:35:34,480
really have anything to do with Ma Guowen's case?

869
00:35:35,039 --> 00:35:36,519
That was all information

870
00:35:37,159 --> 00:35:38,039
I just supplemented later.

871
00:35:39,599 --> 00:35:40,320
When we work a case,

872
00:35:40,320 --> 00:35:41,840
aren't we supposed to piece together

873
00:35:41,840 --> 00:35:42,679
all the information?

874
00:35:42,719 --> 00:35:43,599
As they say,

875
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:44,960
follow every single trace,

876
00:35:45,440 --> 00:35:45,960
and pan for gold in the sand.

877
00:35:45,960 --> 00:35:46,519
Alright, alright, alright.

878
00:35:52,199 --> 00:35:53,119
Having an imagination

879
00:35:53,800 --> 00:35:54,360
is a good thing,

880
00:35:55,920 --> 00:35:56,760
but you can't just dream things up,

881
00:35:57,199 --> 00:35:58,039
and you can't make stuff up.

882
00:36:01,519 --> 00:36:02,079
Another thing,

883
00:36:02,599 --> 00:36:03,519
watch your attitude

884
00:36:04,239 --> 00:36:06,719
when you question witnesses.

885
00:36:09,559 --> 00:36:10,679
You know what I'm talking about, right?

886
00:36:10,840 --> 00:36:11,480
Got it.

887
00:36:12,760 --> 00:36:13,719
You can't jump to conclusions.

888
00:36:19,199 --> 00:36:20,159
"Got relatives in Lacheng?"

889
00:36:21,880 --> 00:36:22,920
"Haven't got a girlfriend or something?"

890
00:36:27,239 --> 00:36:28,320
The dead don't speak.

891
00:36:30,719 --> 00:36:31,960
I'm not talking about you.

892
00:36:32,679 --> 00:36:33,920
I mean the dead don't speak,

893
00:36:33,920 --> 00:36:35,880
and criminals won't just talk to us.

894
00:36:36,440 --> 00:36:38,400
So on a case, you've got to be patient and meticulous.

895
00:36:38,519 --> 00:36:41,199
Pan for gold from every trace of evidence.

896
00:36:41,639 --> 00:36:42,000
Right.

897
00:36:44,800 --> 00:36:45,920
"Right," my ass.

898
00:36:46,880 --> 00:36:48,159
You just said that earlier, didn't you?

899
00:36:48,400 --> 00:36:49,559
Those weren't my words.

900
00:36:49,599 --> 00:36:51,400
Brother Qiang used to say that to me all the time.

901
00:36:53,119 --> 00:36:53,519
Fine.

902
00:36:53,800 --> 00:36:54,599
Your Brother Qiang.

903
00:36:55,119 --> 00:36:55,760
Your Brother Qiang.

904
00:36:56,639 --> 00:36:57,519
Brother Chuang.

905
00:36:58,880 --> 00:37:00,400
Brother Qiang even told me to say hello to you.

906
00:37:01,639 --> 00:37:02,840
Say hello to me?

907
00:37:03,440 --> 00:37:04,719
I'd be lucky if he weren't badmouthing me.

908
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:07,280
He won a Class-Three Merit.

909
00:37:07,880 --> 00:37:08,800
I'm a nobody.

910
00:37:11,280 --> 00:37:12,400
You won a Class-Three Merit too, right?

911
00:37:13,760 --> 00:37:15,000
I was just riding his coattails.

912
00:37:15,400 --> 00:37:17,599
It was a unit citation with Brother Qiang.

913
00:37:17,920 --> 00:37:20,000
A unit citation is still a Class-Three Merit.

914
00:37:21,840 --> 00:37:22,639
Well, that's just great.

915
00:37:23,400 --> 00:37:25,320
You could win a Class-Three Merit with Brother Qiang,

916
00:37:25,760 --> 00:37:27,440
but you won't get squat with me.

917
00:37:28,159 --> 00:37:28,719
What a pity.

918
00:37:32,039 --> 00:37:33,920
Bro, stop giving me grief, will you?

919
00:37:41,880 --> 00:37:42,280
Done eating?

920
00:37:42,960 --> 00:37:43,320
Done.

921
00:37:44,320 --> 00:37:44,760
Listen,

922
00:37:45,679 --> 00:37:46,960
go and warm up

923
00:37:47,199 --> 00:37:47,719
the car.

924
00:37:48,519 --> 00:37:49,320
I'll be right out after a phone call.

925
00:37:50,519 --> 00:37:51,159
Check, please!

926
00:37:51,199 --> 00:37:51,800
No, don't.

927
00:37:52,400 --> 00:37:52,960
I've got this.

928
00:37:54,199 --> 00:37:55,800
My treat for our Class-Three Merit hero.

929
00:37:57,440 --> 00:37:57,840
Thanks.

930
00:37:57,840 --> 00:37:58,519
Thanks, Brother Chuang.

931
00:38:49,280 --> 00:38:49,719
Come on.

932
00:38:50,159 --> 00:38:50,559
No, no, no.

933
00:38:51,079 --> 00:38:51,559
That's not it.

934
00:38:51,920 --> 00:38:52,480
Yan'er, Yan'er.

935
00:38:52,679 --> 00:38:53,440
Well... look, I...

936
00:38:53,880 --> 00:38:54,639
I asked you over...

937
00:38:54,679 --> 00:38:55,920
not because I wanted to...

938
00:38:56,280 --> 00:38:57,119
do... you know, that.

939
00:38:57,159 --> 00:38:59,199
I... I just wanted to chat.

940
00:38:59,320 --> 00:39:00,440
Have a heart-to-heart.

941
00:39:04,119 --> 00:39:05,119
Just have a chat.

942
00:39:07,280 --> 00:39:08,400
Then come on inside.

943
00:39:08,599 --> 00:39:09,400
Sit down and chat.

944
00:39:09,400 --> 00:39:10,159
Are we gonna talk standing up?

945
00:39:10,760 --> 00:39:11,440
Come on.

946
00:39:34,480 --> 00:39:35,239
We've been

947
00:39:35,559 --> 00:39:36,480
neighbors for years,

948
00:39:37,639 --> 00:39:38,719
and old coworkers too.

949
00:39:39,239 --> 00:39:40,239
Just chatting like this,

950
00:39:41,239 --> 00:39:42,199
why give me money?

951
00:39:43,880 --> 00:39:45,920
Doesn't this take up your time?

952
00:39:46,360 --> 00:39:47,800
Time is money,

953
00:39:47,960 --> 00:39:48,519
right?

954
00:39:51,480 --> 00:39:53,239
Time is all I've got these days.

955
00:39:56,199 --> 00:39:56,800
Let's chat.

956
00:39:57,719 --> 00:39:58,719
What do you want to talk about?

957
00:40:01,719 --> 00:40:02,719
What's the matter?

958
00:40:03,639 --> 00:40:04,960
Sighing and groaning like that.

959
00:40:06,639 --> 00:40:07,679
Who picked on you?

960
00:40:12,920 --> 00:40:14,079
I didn't kill Ma Guowen.

961
00:40:17,119 --> 00:40:18,320
Of course you didn't kill him.

962
00:40:19,000 --> 00:40:19,880
But they don't believe me.

963
00:40:20,480 --> 00:40:21,280
I believe you.

964
00:40:23,119 --> 00:40:24,159
I really wanted to kill him.

965
00:40:25,239 --> 00:40:26,159
But you didn't.

966
00:40:31,679 --> 00:40:32,920
Ma Guowen was an asshole.

967
00:40:34,000 --> 00:40:35,360
He bullied the weak and feared the strong.

968
00:40:36,079 --> 00:40:37,280
Always targeted easy marks.

969
00:40:38,840 --> 00:40:40,599
Back then, I just feared getting laid off.

970
00:40:41,079 --> 00:40:42,519
I didn't even dare claim my refund.

971
00:40:43,159 --> 00:40:44,320
Even then, he wouldn't let me off.

972
00:40:44,320 --> 00:40:45,320
He still told me to get lost.

973
00:40:46,440 --> 00:40:47,000
All right.

974
00:40:47,159 --> 00:40:48,239
Turn the page. It's in the past.

975
00:40:55,000 --> 00:40:56,039
I don't know what it is.

976
00:40:58,000 --> 00:40:59,159
Even though Ma Guowen is dead,

977
00:41:00,679 --> 00:41:01,760
I still can't feel happy.

978
00:41:11,599 --> 00:41:12,800
Ma Guowen

979
00:41:14,199 --> 00:41:16,239
was rotten to the core.

980
00:41:17,599 --> 00:41:18,719
He deserved to die anyway.

981
00:41:20,679 --> 00:41:23,239
If I'd known the police would treat me like a killer,

982
00:41:24,119 --> 00:41:25,039
I might as well have just...

983
00:41:25,119 --> 00:41:25,679
killed...

984
00:41:26,679 --> 00:41:27,119
Yeah.

985
00:41:28,039 --> 00:41:28,840
Over ten years ago,

986
00:41:28,880 --> 00:41:29,800
I already wanted to kill him.

987
00:41:35,239 --> 00:41:36,000
All right, that's enough.

988
00:41:38,440 --> 00:41:39,639
Don't let it eat away at you.

989
00:41:40,559 --> 00:41:41,400
The police

990
00:41:41,679 --> 00:41:42,280
are investigating,

991
00:41:42,360 --> 00:41:42,840
right?

992
00:41:43,199 --> 00:41:44,800
Of course they'll question people.

993
00:41:45,719 --> 00:41:47,079
You're not the only one they brought in.

994
00:41:48,039 --> 00:41:49,480
Old Qian was questioned too.

995
00:41:56,000 --> 00:41:56,840
How about this?

996
00:41:58,840 --> 00:42:00,599
Tomorrow I'll grab Cheng Youtian,

997
00:42:00,639 --> 00:42:01,800
Haipeng, and Tieping.

998
00:42:02,159 --> 00:42:03,480
We'll hold up big signs

999
00:42:03,480 --> 00:42:04,599
right outside the police station and shout:

1000
00:42:05,320 --> 00:42:06,719
"Cao Jun is a good man!"

1001
00:42:06,840 --> 00:42:08,239
"Cao Jun didn't kill anyone!"

1002
00:42:08,320 --> 00:42:09,239
"Cao Jun is innocent!"

1003
00:42:09,239 --> 00:42:10,199
Shh, keep it down.

1004
00:42:10,400 --> 00:42:10,760
Don't shout.

1005
00:42:10,800 --> 00:42:12,039
Why are you yelling in the middle of the night?

1006
00:42:12,280 --> 00:42:13,119
Everyone can hear.

1007
00:42:13,639 --> 00:42:14,440
It looks bad.

1008
00:42:23,599 --> 00:42:24,079
Wait,

1009
00:42:24,599 --> 00:42:27,039
don't really go holding signs tomorrow.

1010
00:42:27,280 --> 00:42:28,920
Are you... really going to hold signs and shout?

1011
00:42:30,559 --> 00:42:31,400
You can't go!

1012
00:42:32,320 --> 00:42:33,199
Do you think I'm stupid?

1013
00:42:33,199 --> 00:42:34,039
Like I'd really go?

1014
00:42:34,440 --> 00:42:35,679
I'm not clueless like you.

1015
00:42:37,199 --> 00:42:37,679
Right.

1016
00:42:37,800 --> 00:42:39,239
I knew you wouldn't go.

1017
00:42:44,000 --> 00:42:45,199
Can you sleep now?

1018
00:42:47,639 --> 00:42:48,440
Then let's sleep.

1019
00:42:52,719 --> 00:42:53,480
How am I supposed to sleep?

1020
00:42:54,599 --> 00:42:55,559
Lie down and sleep!

1021
00:44:16,440 --> 00:44:17,400
At 7:30 this morning,

1022
00:44:17,400 --> 00:44:18,920
a worker from Lapi Brewery reported it.

1023
00:44:19,039 --> 00:44:20,559
He said this tuk-tuk belongs to Cao Jun.

1024
00:44:20,760 --> 00:44:21,760
Preliminary examination shows

1025
00:44:21,760 --> 00:44:23,440
the victim died of asphyxiation.

1026
00:44:23,800 --> 00:44:25,360
Whoever killed Cao Jun...

1027
00:44:26,119 --> 00:44:27,360
will die a horrible death.

1028
00:44:27,559 --> 00:44:29,000
Anyone who wanted to kill Cao Jun

1029
00:44:29,880 --> 00:44:31,239
definitely wouldn't kill Ma Guowen.

1030
00:44:32,360 --> 00:44:33,599
Who are you really?

1031
00:44:35,199 --> 00:44:37,039
What's your connection to Liu Xuemei?
